{"ref":"BDB, בָּזָא","hw":"בָּזָא","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">בָּזָא</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. divide, cut through (</strong>? cf. Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּזַע</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܙܰܥ</span> <em>cleave</em><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  Pf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּֽזְאוּ נהרים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 18:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.18.2\">Is 18:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 18:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.18.7\">7</a> whose land <em>rivers cut through</em> (of Cush).","next":"BDB, בָּזָה","prev":"BDB, בַּז"}